{"name":"Orchid Kiss","hex":"#ac74a4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"},{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid","wikidata":"Q25308"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss","wikidata":"Q7307"},{"title":"Orchid (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Orchid is a bright rich purple color that resembles the color which various orchids often exhibit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Labiata.jpg/330px-Labiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid_(color)","wikidata":"Q1925148"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Orchidaceae.png/500px-Orchidaceae.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Orchidaceae.png/1280px-Orchidaceae.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Orchidaceae.png/500px-Orchidaceae.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm